/-
The 4D continuum Yang–Mills existence hypothesis, as an EXPLICIT Lean
structure — the honest alternative to a `True` stub.

# What this module is

This module states, as a single content-bearing Lean `structure`, the
Osterwalder–Schrader (OS) existence assumption for the 4D continuum
Yang–Mills measure `μ_∞`: the precise list of properties a candidate
continuum measure must satisfy for OS reconstruction to produce a
quantum field theory with a positive Hamiltonian, a unique vacuum, and a
mass gap.

**This hypothesis IS the Clay Millennium Problem.**  It is ASSUMED here,
never proven.  This file contains NO proof of existence, NO `sorry`
standing for one, and makes NO claim of closure.  The deliverable is the
*statement* — so that the final mass-gap theorem (`ym_mass_gap_of_existence`
below) can take it as a transparent, explicit hypothesis instead of an
opaque `True` placeholder.  See `docs/4d-existence-hypothesis.md` for the
honest status map (what is rigorously proven in the literature, and what
is open).

# How it is built from the existing repo interfaces

`ContinuumYMExistence` does NOT reinvent the OS axioms.  It BUNDLES the
already-content-bearing OS-axiom predicates from `OSAxioms.lean`:

  * `os_axioms : OSAxiomBundle μ_inf` — the existing record carrying the
    five content predicates `IsOS0 … IsOS4ClusterProperty` (regularity,
    Euclidean/hypercubic invariance, reflection positivity, symmetry,
    clustering) together with their content data (heat-kernel parameter,
    observable algebra + probability functional, symmetry `ObsHom`s,
    finite-volume spectral model + gap rate).

On top of that bundle it adds the four properties that distinguish the
*Yang–Mills* continuum existence problem from the bare OS-axiom skeleton,
each carried as a genuine `Prop` predicate (never `True`):

  * `os1_o4_restoration` — full continuum O(4) ⋉ ℝ⁴ Euclidean invariance,
    i.e. the **O(4) rotation-restoration** content (the lattice only has
    the hypercubic subgroup H₄ ⊂ O(4); restoration of the full rotation
    group in the continuum limit is the genuine open analysis,
    Magnen–Rivasseau–Sénéor).
  * `gauge_content` — the Schwinger functions are generated by
    gauge-invariant local polynomials in the curvature `F` (the theory is
    a *gauge* theory, not a generic scalar field).
  * `uv_asymptotic_freedom` — the correct short-distance / ultraviolet
    behaviour (asymptotic freedom: the running coupling vanishes
    logarithmically at short distances).
  * `nontrivial` — the measure is genuinely interacting (not Gaussian /
    not the free field): the theory is non-trivial.

The four predicates are abstract `Prop`s parameterized by the same
underlying `ContinuumMeasure`, in the same style as the abstract Prop
laws of `OSReconstruction.lean` (`HamiltonianNonneg`, etc.): the FULL
analytic content of each is open mathematics, so we expose a *named*
predicate the hypothesis must supply, rather than a `True` that hides the
obligation.  This is deliberate: the value of the structure is that every
conjunct the Clay problem requires appears, by name, as a field that an
inhabitant must produce — none is silently discharged.

# The derived mass gap

`ContinuumYMWithGap` extends `ContinuumYMExistence` with the OS
reconstruction data (`OSReconstruction μ_inf`, the Hilbert space +
Hamiltonian + vacuum + semigroup of `OSReconstruction.lean`) and the
spectral-gap conclusion `HasSpectralGapAt rec m_0` at a constructive-real
rate `m_0 > 0`.  `ym_mass_gap_of_existence` then exhibits the mass-gap
statement as a transparent consequence of the explicit hypothesis: GIVEN
a `ContinuumYMWithGap`, the OS-reconstructed Hamiltonian has a positive
spectral gap.  The hypothesis is consumed as an argument — it is NEVER
proven here.

